WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
01 · OVERVIEW: Evaluate claims systematically instead of guessing. High share counts show attention—never scholarly accuracy or verified proof.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
02 · LATERAL READ: Open new tabs to check the source's reputation. Don't judge an unfamiliar site solely from its own "About Us" page.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
03 · TRACE DATA: Follow links back to the original primary study. Compare headline claims against actual methodology, sample size, and year.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
04 · CRAAP LENS: Check Currency, Relevance, Authority, Accuracy, Purpose. Separate factual reporting from opinion essays, lobbying, and native ads.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
05 · CITATION: Record author, year, title & URL while taking notes. Paraphrasing another person's idea without attribution is still plagiarism.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
06 · TRY IT: Trace one viral statistic back to its original dataset. Verify publication date and two independent reliable confirmations first.
